Playwright Chromium sandbox seccomp profile

Source: https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/v1.62.1/utils/docker/seccomp_profile.json
Release: v1.62.1
Commit: 26a9e470a7b3c7822084b09fb7f13902c5f37b51
Upstream SHA-256: cc3e61cabda6bbc1e53e54d27ba4d55a9d3be829b6dd1a596f4a7b31b1cc7849
Local SHA-256: 8ca5a597870cd458f1ddbd0b1593bce25a7763c05487849283a731c62a13e662
Licence: Apache License 2.0 (see PLAYWRIGHT-LICENSE)
Modifications:

- The `chroot` rule is unconditional so Chromium can finish its own
  unprivileged user-namespace sandbox while the fixture keeps every container
  capability dropped. The upstream rule is conditional on `CAP_SYS_CHROOT`,
  which Docker removes from the loaded profile when Compose applies
  `cap_drop: [ALL]`.
- `faccessat2` is allowed. runc's container init needs it (Docker Engine
  29.8.2 fails to start the container without it), and Docker's default
  profile allows it. The profile already allows `faccessat`.
- `open_tree` through `pidfd_getfd` (syscalls 428 to 438) are denied with
  `ENOSYS`. runc answers `ENOSYS` only for syscalls newer than the newest one
  a profile names, so naming `faccessat2` would otherwise turn their answer
  into `EPERM`, and glibc stops falling back from `clone3` to `clone`.

The profile is fixture-only. It extends Docker's default seccomp policy with
the user-namespace syscalls required by Playwright's non-root Chromium sandbox.
